From 6fbe7f86ab2ccc133279826c396a6fd328973053 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:32:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Apple Silicon: run the x86_64 build under Rosetta 2

- patch guest FS accesses to GS/TSD slots when there is no LDT (fs_patcher)
- Rosetta-aware TLS mode selection (DC_TLS=ldt|patch)
- x86-64-v2 baseline instead of -march=native on Apple Silicon, Intel Homebrew prefix
- calibrate the TSC frequency instead of reading machdep.tsc.frequency
- Shared instead of Managed textures on unified memory
- Linux test harness for the FS patcher
